 on node1 (Ubuntu 16.04). Installed aide/aide-common, verified the packaged Debian/Ubuntu AIDE config recursively applies full content checksums (SHA256/SHA512/RMD160/TIGER/HAVAL/GOST/CRC32 + metadata) to /etc via the \\\"/ Full\\\" catch-all rule (with narrow, pre-existing exceptions for known-volatile files like resolv.conf/adjtime), initialized the baseline database at /var/lib/aide/aide.db (70,149 entries), and proved detection works end-to-end by tampering with /etc/hosts, running aide --check, observing the exact checksum/size/mtime diff reported, then restoring /etc/hosts and re-baselining to a clean state. The distro's /etc/cron.daily/aide job (already enabled) will run these checks automatically going forward and report changes. Completed the mandatory restart-evidence protocol on node1: captured pre-restart boot_id and a clean /etc AIDE check, issued a background `reboot` so the ack returned before disconnect, polled until exec access returned, confirmed boot_id changed (a1dc8e25... -> 2e616fe5...), and confirmed post-restart that the AIDE database file was intact (same md5) and a fresh aide --check showed zero differences under real /etc paths (all reported diffs were in /run, lxcfs cgroup pseudo-files from ephemeral SSH sessions, or postfix's chroot copies under /var/spool/postfix/etc, none in /etc itself).\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Inspected node1 OS/environment and confirmed AIDE package availability\",\"Installed aide and aide-common via apt\",\"Reviewed AIDE config (/etc/aide/aide.conf and aide.conf.d/*) to confirm /etc is covered by full content-checksum monitoring\",\"Ran aideinit to build the initial AIDE database for /etc/ (and full filesystem) baseline\",\"Verified the active database (/var/lib/aide/aide.db) matches the freshly generated one\",\"Ran aide.wrapper --check to confirm a clean baseline with zero /etc differences\",\"Tampered with /etc/hosts (appended a marker line) and re-ran aide.wrapper --check to prove detection of the change with full checksum diff output\",\"Restored /etc/hosts to its original content and re-ran aideinit to re-baseline to the clean state\",\"Confirmed /etc/cron.daily/aide (daily automated check+report) is present and cron.service is enabled/active\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id and a clean baseline check as restart evidence\",\"Issued a backgrounded `sudo reboot` on node1 so the acknowledgement returned before disconnection\",\"Polled node1 until exec access returned after the restart\",\"Verified boot_id changed post-restart, confirming a genuine reboot\",\"Verified AIDE database file integrity (checksum) and cron service health post-restart\",\"Ran a post-restart aide.wrapper --check and confirmed zero differences within real /etc paths\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"AIDE installed and configured to monitor /etc with content-level integrity checks\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-61c6bfaa218543dd\",\"cmd-7fbedb24b562407f\",\"cmd-69237d34f3e34a7d\",\"cmd-41d6d76fa7d8426d\",\"cmd-70a9894985494c90\",\"cmd-291493f576714429\",\"cmd-6c13e1587b3e45b5\",\"cmd-3263ada1e0774463\",\"cmd-fe3074aa6ee64384\"],\"summary\":\"Confirmed Ubuntu 16.04 node1, installed aide/aide-common, and confirmed via aide.conf.d that /etc is monitored recursively with full checksums (SHA256/SHA512/etc.) via the top-level '/ Full' rule, with only known-volatile files (resolv.conf, adjtime, etc.) exempted.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline database initialized and in place at the configured active path\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3c94e2193a9841dc\",\"cmd-e0d04c57f65f484f\",\"cmd-ea53787a648248b6\",\"cmd-f0a7ac90e7b34339\",\"cmd-d9cca889f60140f5\"],\"summary\":\"Ran aideinit; produced /var/lib/aide/aide.db with 70,149 entries; confirmed aide.db and aide.db.new have identical md5sums, i.e. the baseline is correctly installed as the active database.\"},{\"requirement\":\"Baseline correctly reflects a clean, healthy /etc state (no false positives)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2179fd872726494a\",\"cmd-8258fb17d7e64131\",